===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ḱerh₂-}}

{{lbor|en|la|cerebellum}}, diminutive of {{m|la|cerebrum}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌsɛ.ɹɪˈbɛl.əm/|a=RP}}
{{rfap|en}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌsɛɹ.əˈbɛl.əm/|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛləm|s=4}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|+|cerebella}}

# {{lb|en|neuroanatomy}} Part of the [[hindbrain]] in [[vertebrate]]s. In [[human]]s it lies between the [[brainstem]] and the back of the [[cerebrum]] and is formed of two [[lateral]] [[lobe]]s and a [[median]] lobe. It plays an important role in [[sensory]] [[perception]], [[motor]] output, [[balance]] and [[posture]].
#: {{syn|en|parencephalon}}
#: {{holo|en|hindbrain}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=w:Bill Bryson|title=The Body: A Guide for Occupants|publisher=Black Swan|page=61|text=Although the '''cerebellum''' occupies just 10 per cent of the cranial cavity, it has more than half the brain’s neurons.}}

